1
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:39,840
Attention, everyone. Get ready!

2
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,600
Captain, why did we stop?

3
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:48,600
The enemy's firepower

4
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:50,320
has been suppressing us heavily from the southeast.

5
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:52,160
They want to drive us toward the southwest.

6
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:53,760
But the recon squad just reported

7
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,960
that they've taken out their heavy firepower.

8
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:57,840
Now, everyone, listen to my orders.

9
00:01:58,240 --> 00:01:59,680
Move the troops toward the southeast!

10
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:00,680
Increase firepower and break out!

11
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:01,520
Yes, sir. Let's go!

12
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:07,760
What's going on?

13
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:10,000
Have we been exposed?

14
00:02:10,199 --> 00:02:10,840
I don't think so.

15
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:12,440
If we had been spotted,

16
00:02:12,440 --> 00:02:13,440
they would've shelled us by now.

17
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:14,760
No way.

18
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:16,000
We have an easy target right in front of us.

19
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:17,400
We can't just let them get away like this.

20
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:19,680
Our comms with the battalion command post

21
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:20,600
have been down for a while now.

22
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:23,160
And the battalion commander ordered us to hold position.

23
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:24,760
Should we wait a bit longer?

24
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:25,760
Wait my ass!

25
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:27,000
If we wait any longer, it'll be too late.

26
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:28,400
All firepower assigned to the 1st Company,

27
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,600
listen to my orders. Attack!

28
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:38,520
Take cover!

29
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:16,800
Captain, the path ahead is blocked by mines.

30
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:18,000
We've sustained heavy losses.

31
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:19,600
Fall back immediately.

32
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:20,800
Break out towards the southwest.

33
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:21,320
Move!

34
00:03:21,320 --> 00:03:21,720
Yes, sir!

35
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:44,480
This is bad!

36
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,240
Xu Dali has turned back.

37
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:47,200
What?

38
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:48,520
Xu Dali has turned back.

39
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,240
This has turned into a total mess.

40
00:03:51,760 --> 00:03:53,560
Quick, find another blocking position!

41
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:54,280
Fall back, now!

42
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:55,080
Fall back!

43
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:00,840
Sir!

44
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:03,520
I apologize, commanders.

45
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:05,920
With the battle reaching this point,

46
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:07,720
I've embarrassed myself.

47
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:10,240
Comrade Suo Jian'an,

48
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:11,160
please take a seat first.

49
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:12,040
Yes, sir.

50
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:16,279
Chicken stewed with mushrooms...

51
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:18,959
It only absorbs the flavor when stewed long enough.

52
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:20,240
Right, Dean Chen?

53
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,000
If you ask me,

54
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:25,520
the heat is just right.

55
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:28,120
The timing is perfect.

56
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,640
The meat looks delicious,

57
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:31,800
and the seasoning is balanced.

58
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:34,080
Yes, Chief.

59
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:35,400
Right now, all the ingredients

60
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,640
are stewing in the same pot.

61
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,240
Not a drop of juice will be lost.

62
00:04:40,960 --> 00:04:41,520
Sir!

63
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:45,240
Chief, both sides are evenly matched right now.

64
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:46,760
Should we let them continue like this

65
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:47,760
and fight to the last man,

66
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:48,800
or end it in a draw?

67
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:50,800
Make the call yourself.

68
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,160
Of course,

69
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:54,240
you can also consult the two battalion commanders.

70
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:55,600
Sir!

71
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:56,840
Chief!

72
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,280
I believe Guo Zijian severely violated the rules.

73
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:00,480
I refuse to accept a draw.

74
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:03,360
Don't come to me about rule violations.

75
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:04,640
Ask Staff Officer Liang.

76
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:06,560
Battalion Commander Jiang,

77
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,800
may I ask what violation you are referring to?

78
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:12,000
A hundred men is a company's formation at most.

79
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,480
But judging from the firepower,

80
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:15,840
Guo Zijian has thrown in nearly half a battalion.

81
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,000
Squad Leader Hong,

82
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:20,720
put the troop distribution map for both sides

83
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:21,640
on the big screen.

84
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:22,040
Yes, sir.

85
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:30,120
Both sides have a hundred troops engaged.

86
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:32,320
But the configuration of personnel and equipment

87
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,360
is fundamentally different.

88
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:35,680
The 2nd Battalion is based on the existing

89
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,360
Xu Dali Infantry Company,

90
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:39,200
with some main battle firepower attached for support.

91
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:40,200
Meanwhile, the 1st Battalion

92
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:42,520
is entirely based on firepower strike effectiveness.

93
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:44,400
It's equivalent to temporarily forming a

94
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:45,360
new combined force.

95
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:46,800
A new combined force?

96
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:47,880
What do you mean?

97
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:50,600
It means that although the troop count is small,

98
00:05:50,680 --> 00:05:52,120
the firepower is complete.

99
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,080
To tell you the truth,

100
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,880
if we weren't limited by

101
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:58,440
the inability to contact attached service branches,

102
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,080
to attack your 2nd Battalion's position,

103
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:03,640
I'm afraid even fighter jets and long-range missiles

104
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:04,200
could be called in.

105
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:08,920
Isn't that right, Staff Officer Liang?

106
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:11,200
Actually, this force composition isn't new.

107
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:13,520
It has appeared in actual combat many times.

108
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:14,800
Just this year,

109
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,480
in a combat operation in the Middle East,

110
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:18,640
it even had a relatively mature organization,

111
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:20,560
known as a Battalion Combat Group.

112
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:21,880
You know about this too?

113
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,280
Our Staff Officer Liang,

114
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:25,920
although her major is military communication engineering,

115
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:29,440
the scope of her knowledge

116
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:31,680
extends far beyond just this field.

117
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:33,680
Fine.

118
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:35,480
So according to what you're saying,

119
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:36,920
if our 2nd Battalion

120
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:39,880
could also deploy the same force composition,

121
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,880
the result wouldn't be like this at all.

122
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:43,640
This is simply unfair!

123
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,960
What do you mean unfair?

124
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:46,800
At the meeting, Staff Officer Liang

125
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,320
made the rules very clear.

126
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:49,720
We must base our tactics on

127
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:51,600
the combined battalion's existing equipment and personnel.

128
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:53,840
We didn't step outside of that scope.

129
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:56,080
You can't, just because you didn't think of it,

130
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,840
blame others for going faster and further.

131
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:00,000
Guo Zijian, are you playing word games with me?

132
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:01,480
Stop arguing!

133
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:05,600
The battle isn't over yet.

134
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:09,760
Sit down.

135
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:11,680
Report.

136
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:12,960
Speak.

137
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:14,080
Commander.

138
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:16,880
Just now, while the two battalion commanders were discussing,

139
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:18,480
the battle situation became quite clear.

140
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:19,880
What do you mean?

141
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:21,240
Squad Leader Hong.

142
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:21,840
Yes, sir.

143
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:24,400
Reporting to the commanders,

144
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:26,480
although the 1st Battalion initially surrounded the 2nd,

145
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:28,520
due to their own firepower and troops

146
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:29,280
being too scattered,

147
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:31,000
and frequent coordination errors,

148
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:32,640
the 2nd Battalion has successfully broken out

149
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:33,840
and executed a counter-encirclement.

150
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:34,320
Currently,

151
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:36,160
they are gradually wearing down the 1st Battalion's remaining forces.

152
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:37,960
The outcome of the battle is basically set.

153
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:40,200
The 2nd Battalion is victorious.

154
00:08:34,679 --> 00:08:36,000
Take care, Dean Chen.

155
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:42,880
Commander.

156
00:08:43,799 --> 00:08:46,040
In this exercise, for Guo Zijian,

157
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:47,680
wasn't it a bit unfair?

158
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:49,080
Why do you say that?

159
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,480
If you hadn't suspended the command posts,

160
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:55,240
the 1st Battalion's offensive looked stronger than the 2nd's.

161
00:08:56,880 --> 00:08:59,200
Jiang Shengqiang was right.

162
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:01,160
Guo Zijian's layout this time

163
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:02,800
was actually a gamble.

164
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,760
A gamble? On what?

165
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:07,800
That Jiang Shengqiang knew nothing about his tactics.

166
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:09,720
Doesn't that just show

167
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:10,880
that his ideas are quite novel?

168
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:14,600
Before Guo Zijian came to the 396th Brigade,

169
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:16,160
one of his research subjects

170
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,040
was on the future combined arms battalion

171
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:19,920
and tactical changes in three-dimensional warfare.

172
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:22,440
This Battalion Combat Group

173
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:24,680
is the core of that subject.

174
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:26,800
Nothing wrong with that. It's good.

175
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,560
So we also wanted to see this Battalion Combat Group

176
00:09:29,880 --> 00:09:31,200
and where its key points really lie.

177
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:33,840
I understand now.

178
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,120
You and Staff Officer Liang

179
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:37,280
specifically set a trap for Guo Zijian.

180
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:38,400
You did it on purpose.

181
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:41,360
True.

182
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:43,840
A combat group of about a hundred men,

183
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:45,080
with divided and scattered forces,

184
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:46,080
and multiple, complex firepower.

185
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:49,080
Its strongest and weakest points depend on command.

186
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:50,000
The deciding factor

187
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:52,320
was entirely focused on Guo Zijian alone.

188
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:55,000
That's why we can't just focus on him alone.

189
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:56,800
We need to look at combined arms.

190
00:09:58,320 --> 00:10:00,040
After that kid Guo Zijian arrived at the 1st Battalion,

191
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:00,960
he wanted to establish his authority in one battle.

192
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:03,520
When this opportunity arose, we gave it to him,

193
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:04,880
to see if he could grasp it.

194
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:07,880
Then why did you ruin his plan halfway through?

195
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:09,080
We just didn't want

196
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,880
him to win so comfortably and easily.

197
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:12,920
This is quite good too.

198
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:15,200
Everyone in the 1st Battalion now knows

199
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:16,360
that by following Guo Zijian,

200
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,960
they have a chance to defeat the 2nd Battalion.

201
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:20,640
Our goal has been achieved.

202
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:21,640
From now on,

203
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:23,800
it's up to Guo Zijian himself.

204
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:26,880
Brilliant, Commander.

205
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:31,400
This After Action Review

206
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:35,080
was supposed to be hosted by the Battalion Commander.

207
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:36,600
But I, Sang Haitian,

208
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,040
as a political cadre

209
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:40,040
who's been Instructor of the 1st Battalion for over three years,

210
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:41,040
volunteered

211
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:44,000
to host this purely military meeting.

212
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,640
Let me say something from the bottom of my heart.

213
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:48,880
Ever since I came to the 1st Battalion,

214
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:50,720
under fair conditions,

215
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:52,200
this was the closest match we've had

216
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:55,160
against the 2nd Battalion.

217
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:58,560
Li Songwei, what do you think?

218
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:02,880
You, as Party Secretary,

219
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:04,680
set the tone for the meeting right away.

220
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:06,720
How can us ordinary folks have a say?

221
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:09,120
Li Songwei,

222
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:11,200
speak your mind.

223
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:12,960
Stop being unreasonable, okay?

224
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:14,600
Fine.

225
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:16,120
I admit,

226
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:19,320
there was indeed some skill in how this battle was fought.

227
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:21,240
But we still lost, didn't we?

228
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:22,040
We lost

229
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:25,520
because after the directing group cut off communications,

230
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:27,120
you

231
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:29,200
missed a great tactical opportunity.

232
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:30,600
In the end, the problem

233
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:32,400
lies with you, Li Songwei.

234
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:34,600
Anyway, the winner takes all.

235
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:36,800
I'm a defeated general,

236
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:38,800
so I can only be your punching bag.

237
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:41,640
Don't be unreasonable with me here, okay?

238
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:43,200
Talk sense if you have a point.

239
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:45,160
All right.

240
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:48,400
Then don't blame me for being blunt.

241
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:50,920
Battalion Commander Guo,

242
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,920
in this show you put on,

243
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:56,840
you didn't explain your core combat ideology

244
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:57,960
to anyone at all.

245
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,520
To put it nicely,

246
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:00,920
you were afraid of leaking information.

247
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:02,480
To put it bluntly,

248
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:04,280
you just lack the most basic trust

249
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:05,400
in us 1st Battalion cadres.

250
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:12,600
Keep going, Company Commander Li.

251
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:14,480
I'm done.

252
00:12:23,920 --> 00:12:25,480
The issue Company Commander Li just raised

253
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:29,000
touches on the core of this exercise.

254
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:29,800
Indeed,

255
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,240
as the commander,

256
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,920
I kept every aspect of this exercise,

257
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:38,400
including Wu Dongsheng's reconnaissance mission,

258
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:41,400
completely in my own hands.

259
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:43,280
And it's true I didn't

260
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:45,160
communicate with you all beforehand.

261
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,680
As for Company Commander Li's criticism today,

262
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:49,320
I humbly accept it,

263
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:51,800
but I absolutely will not change.

264
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:05,280
A commander's battlefield decisions

265
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:08,760
concern the entire battalion's offense and defense.

266
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:10,720
It's impossible for every mission

267
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:13,320
to be briefed to commanders at all levels.

268
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:15,720
I can only say

269
00:13:16,520 --> 00:13:18,480
the directing team has an expert this time.

270
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:21,680
Targeting my tactics and ideas,

271
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:24,840
they pulled off a command post double kill.

272
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:27,840
If we say

273
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,440
the first half was a test

274
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:31,040
of my combat plan,

275
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:32,440
then the second half

276
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:36,680
tested the adaptability of everyone here.

277
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:37,520
Do you have it?

278
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:40,520
Do you have that adaptability?

279
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:43,760
So stop always finding faults in others.

280
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:47,840
Company Commander Li just made a great point.

281
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:50,480
That is, between us,

282
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:52,160
there is no trust.

283
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:55,200
The truth is, before the battle began,

284
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:57,160
there was no foundation of trust either.

285
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:59,240
The directing team saw this too.

286
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:02,360
They saw the trust crisis within the First Battalion,

287
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:04,240
and used it to set up this trap.

288
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:06,160
From what Battalion Commander Guo is saying,

289
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,360
so you want our trust now.

290
00:14:10,040 --> 00:14:11,760
Trust has always been mutual.

291
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:13,480
For the First Battalion

292
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:17,640
to fight well and win every future battle,

293
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:19,800
and reclaim its former glory,

294
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:22,360
there must be trust between us.

295
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:25,040
Without a single shred of doubt.

296
00:14:25,160 --> 00:14:26,320
Easier said than done.

297
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:29,040
Trust requires a foundation.

298
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:30,960
And it comes in different levels.

299
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:33,040
If you want everyone to trust you,

300
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:35,720
you have to show us some real skills.

301
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:39,040
And what counts as real skills?

302
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:40,160
It's very simple.

303
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:42,600
Let's compete in three minor events.

304
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,000
Are you up for it?

305
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:49,800
Squad Leader Wu!

306
00:14:49,840 --> 00:14:50,560
Let's go!

307
00:14:50,880 --> 00:14:51,760
Squad Leader Wu!

308
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:52,560
Let's go!

309
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:04,720
Come on!

310
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:05,360
Squad Leader Wu!

311
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:06,480
Come on!

312
00:15:17,840 --> 00:15:19,840
Squad leader, crush him with your golden right foot!

313
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,160
Got it!

314
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:28,520
Way to go, Old Wu!

315
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:11,520
Battalion Commander.

316
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:13,920
I lost fair and square today.

317
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:14,960
Nice moves.

318
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:18,520
I lost face, but you earned the glory.

319
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:22,440
Ready, begin!

320
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:22,880
See that?

321
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:25,200
That's the new Deputy Battalion Commander.

322
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:29,520
I thought the open Deputy Battalion Commander position

323
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:30,680
would definitely be yours.

324
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:33,360
But who knew they'd transfer someone in from outside.

325
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:38,520
Then again, you did

326
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:39,960
lose two exercises in a row.

327
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,400
It's not a good look,

328
00:18:41,880 --> 00:18:43,000
so it's no wonder.

329
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:06,840
Songwei.

330
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:07,800
Are you okay?

331
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:11,520
Nothing.

332
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:15,560
Just got back from my trip, I'm a bit tired.

333
00:19:15,680 --> 00:19:18,600
Take good care of yourself when I'm not around.

334
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,440
Daddy!

335
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:24,160
Dagou, Xiaoshao.

336
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:26,240
Did you miss me?

337
00:19:26,480 --> 00:19:28,000
We did! We missed you, Daddy!

338
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:29,800
When will we be able to...

339
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:31,640
...come live with you?

340
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:32,720
Soon, very soon.

341
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:35,680
Once Daddy gets some free time...

342
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:37,840
...I'll come back to see you, okay?

343
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,760
Songwei, the kids are starting elementary school soon.

344
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:42,960
What about us moving to the base?

345
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:47,320
Huifen.

346
00:19:47,840 --> 00:19:50,360
We might have to wait a little longer for that.

347
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:52,560
Didn't you say your promotion to Deputy Battalion Commander...

348
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:53,680
...would make it possible?

349
00:19:58,760 --> 00:19:59,960
I'm just not capable enough.

350
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:08,280
Fifty-one.

351
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:09,920
Fifty-two.

352
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:11,480
Fifty-three.

353
00:20:12,800 --> 00:20:13,360
Fifty-four.

354
00:20:14,360 --> 00:20:15,480
We definitely need the training.

355
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:17,040
We embarrassed ourselves big time today.

356
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:17,920
Hold on.

357
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:19,840
What are you talking about?

358
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:21,160
What's so embarrassing about that?

359
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:22,320
Our Battalion Commander is awesome.

360
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:23,520
We should be happy.

361
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:24,680
Right, Squad Leader?

362
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:25,680
Exactly.

363
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:28,760
It's been so long since I've felt this way.

364
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:29,920
What feeling, Squad Leader?

365
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:31,600
The feeling of being a recruit.

366
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:32,360
You know...

367
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:34,400
That feeling of wanting to charge into battle.

368
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:36,480
That feeling of your blood boiling.

369
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:38,040
The kind that just feels incredibly thrilling.

370
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:39,720
Just a super, super hyped-up feeling.

371
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:40,160
Exactly.

372
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:43,080
Squad Leader.

373
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:44,040
All right.

374
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:44,440
All right, Squad Leader.

375
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:44,920
Let me feel your forehead.

376
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:45,400
That's enough.

377
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:46,560
Get out of here.

378
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,640
It's not a fever, I'm just fired up!

379
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:50,640
By the way, Huzi.

380
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:53,320
Our Battalion Commander's skills are no joke.

381
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:55,320
I exchanged a few blows with him today.

382
00:20:56,240 --> 00:20:56,760
Pretty impressive.

383
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:59,600
Yeah, he pinned you to the ground in a chokehold.

384
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:01,360
So you know he's "pretty impressive."

385
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:03,040
What do you know?

386
00:21:05,080 --> 00:21:06,360
This time, our First Battalion...

387
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:08,280
...will finally get its day in the sun.

388
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:11,120
Did you hear what the Squad Leader said?

389
00:21:11,360 --> 00:21:12,760
The First Battalion is going to shine.

390
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:15,000
Which means I'm going to shine.

391
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:16,720
When that happens...

392
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:19,160
...once our Squad Leader becomes a Platoon Leader...

393
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:22,160
...won't that leave an open spot?

394
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:23,480
Then wouldn't I...

395
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:26,240
...become what?

396
00:21:26,840 --> 00:21:28,240
Squad Leader Lin.

397
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:29,720
When that time comes, I'm telling you...

398
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:30,240
...my girlfriend...

399
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:32,360
...will definitely come from our hometown to marry me.

400
00:21:32,520 --> 00:21:35,720
I'll treat you guys to all the wedding drinks and candy you want.

401
00:21:37,280 --> 00:21:38,240
You two.

402
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:40,440
Let me see what it feels like to be Squad Leader.

403
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:41,440
Gentlemen.

404
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:42,760
Stand up!

405
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:44,840
At ease!

406
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:46,720
Attention!

407
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:50,200
Call me Squad Leader just to humor me.

408
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:52,840
Baby face.

409
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:54,480
Show some respect.

410
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:56,000
What are you two talking about?

411
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:57,240
All right.

412
00:21:57,600 --> 00:21:58,120
Stop fooling around.

413
00:21:58,440 --> 00:21:59,480
Save your energy for physical training.

414
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:01,040
Physical training!

415
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:05,240
Push-ups, ready!

416
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:30,280
One, two, three, four!

417
00:22:30,640 --> 00:22:32,560
One, two, three... four!

418
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,640
One, two, three... four!

419
00:22:34,960 --> 00:22:37,720
One, two, one!

420
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:40,720
One, two, three, four!

421
00:22:41,760 --> 00:22:42,760
One, two, one!

422
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:44,360
One, two, one!

423
00:22:44,680 --> 00:22:47,440
One, two, three, four!

424
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:50,040
One, two, three, four!

425
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:52,320
One, two, three... four!

426
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:54,440
One, two, three... four!

427
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:58,880
One, two, one!

428
00:23:00,360 --> 00:23:01,680
Five kilometers!

429
00:23:01,760 --> 00:23:02,720
Oh, how I love you!

430
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:04,280
If I miss a day,

431
00:23:04,280 --> 00:23:05,560
I miss you like crazy!

432
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:07,720
These soldiers of yours...

433
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:10,240
...are actually quite endearing when they get serious.

434
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:14,720
Five kilometers!

435
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:16,040
Oh, how I love you!

436
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:17,520
If I miss a day,

437
00:23:17,560 --> 00:23:18,720
I miss you like crazy!

438
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,240
It seems these soldiers...

439
00:23:22,400 --> 00:23:25,040
...have started to accept their battalion commander.

440
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:27,240
One, two, three, four!

441
00:23:27,640 --> 00:23:31,520
One, two, three, four!

442
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:36,080
One, two, one!

443
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:46,760
The next phase's training plan submitted by the First Battalion...

444
00:23:46,760 --> 00:23:47,280
Did you read it?

445
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:48,480
I did.

446
00:23:49,600 --> 00:23:51,520
We've just never done it this way before.

447
00:23:51,520 --> 00:23:52,560
Will it work?

448
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:56,040
Young people are bold in thought and action.

449
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:57,280
As leaders,

450
00:23:57,560 --> 00:23:59,960
we should provide a platform and fully support them.

451
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:03,120
Lao Suo, give him this chance.

452
00:24:03,280 --> 00:24:04,880
Give him a little more time.

453
00:24:05,520 --> 00:24:06,440
Let's see the results first.

454
00:24:07,600 --> 00:24:10,000
They lost to the Second Battalion this time.

455
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:12,880
I'm worried he might resort to unorthodox methods...

456
00:24:13,440 --> 00:24:14,200
...and just make things worse.

457
00:24:15,840 --> 00:24:17,520
I wouldn't be so sure about that.

458
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:19,320
This Guo Zijian...

459
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:23,160
Lao Suo, I stand by what I said.

460
00:24:23,320 --> 00:24:24,080
We must always...

461
00:24:24,080 --> 00:24:27,560
...maintain a perspective of trust, appreciation, and development...

462
00:24:27,560 --> 00:24:29,080
...towards every officer and soldier.

463
00:24:30,320 --> 00:24:32,760
All right. Since the Commissar says so.

464
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:33,840
It's decided.

465
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:35,920
Think back to when we were young.

466
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:37,480
We went all out to get things done.

467
00:24:37,480 --> 00:24:39,040
We were terrified of falling behind.

468
00:24:39,120 --> 00:24:40,000
Yes.

469
00:24:40,360 --> 00:24:41,040
Fortunately...

470
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:44,320
...we met leaders who understood and supported us.

471
00:24:44,320 --> 00:24:45,560
That's how we got to where we are today.

472
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:46,600
Exactly.

473
00:24:46,640 --> 00:24:48,920
We must pass on and carry forward this spirit.

474
00:24:49,240 --> 00:24:50,200
Well said, Commissar.

475
00:24:51,640 --> 00:24:52,080
I'll be going now.

476
00:24:52,080 --> 00:24:52,600
Then it's settled.

477
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:53,560
All right, all right.

478
00:25:02,080 --> 00:25:04,920
I've gathered all the officers and key personnel today

479
00:25:05,360 --> 00:25:06,840
to announce three things.

480
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:08,040
First.

481
00:25:08,520 --> 00:25:10,200
With the approval of the brigade party committee,

482
00:25:10,480 --> 00:25:12,240
there will be a few officer position adjustments

483
00:25:12,760 --> 00:25:13,840
for a period of two months.

484
00:25:14,520 --> 00:25:15,080
Among them,

485
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:16,720
First Company Commander Li Songwei

486
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:19,280
will temporarily serve as a battalion staff officer.

487
00:25:21,040 --> 00:25:22,000
Second.

488
00:25:22,480 --> 00:25:24,480
The battalion will use the armed recon squad as the core

489
00:25:25,040 --> 00:25:26,320
to establish a Blue Force detachment.

490
00:25:27,120 --> 00:25:28,760
Wu Dongsheng will be the detachment leader,

491
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:32,720
but for now, Staff Officer Li Songwei is in charge.

492
00:25:33,920 --> 00:25:34,840
Third.

493
00:25:35,680 --> 00:25:36,840
As you can all see,

494
00:25:37,240 --> 00:25:38,920
there are many charts posted up here.

495
00:25:39,720 --> 00:25:43,280
They are training standards for nearly 30 specialties.

496
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:45,320
But these standards

497
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:46,880
aren't from the syllabus.

498
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:48,480
Report!

499
00:25:49,120 --> 00:25:49,560
Speak.

500
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:52,040
Training by the syllabus is a higher-up mandate.

501
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:53,480
Is it okay not to follow it?

502
00:25:53,880 --> 00:25:57,200
Training by the syllabus is a basic rule we must follow.

503
00:25:58,000 --> 00:25:59,920
But the charts I've posted

504
00:26:00,480 --> 00:26:02,640
are a three-tier standard I worked hard to find.

505
00:26:03,080 --> 00:26:03,800
The first tier

506
00:26:04,920 --> 00:26:07,760
is the training record of our 396th Brigade.

507
00:26:08,240 --> 00:26:09,000
I took a look,

508
00:26:09,960 --> 00:26:11,560
and most of them belong to the Second Battalion.

509
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:12,960
The second tier

510
00:26:14,160 --> 00:26:16,000
is the record of our Group Army.

511
00:26:16,920 --> 00:26:18,560
This standard is a bit high,

512
00:26:18,640 --> 00:26:20,480
but it's attainable if we push ourselves.

513
00:26:20,960 --> 00:26:21,720
The third tier

514
00:26:22,480 --> 00:26:23,960
is the record of the entire Army.

515
00:26:24,520 --> 00:26:27,320
For this record, without working to the bone,

516
00:26:27,520 --> 00:26:29,200
no one will easily surpass it.

517
00:26:29,880 --> 00:26:33,240
I know some people might think

518
00:26:33,920 --> 00:26:37,200
the Second Battalion is our biggest military obstacle.

519
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:39,440
But I'm telling you,

520
00:26:39,960 --> 00:26:43,040
defeating the Second Battalion isn't our ultimate goal.

521
00:26:43,280 --> 00:26:44,800
I posted these charts up here

522
00:26:44,800 --> 00:26:48,560
to demand that if you have the skill and the grit,

523
00:26:48,840 --> 00:26:51,160
you put in the work toward these records.

524
00:26:52,520 --> 00:26:53,560
In two more months,

525
00:26:54,120 --> 00:26:56,400
we'll have the Group Army's combat exercise.

526
00:26:57,400 --> 00:27:00,400
When that time comes, I hope our First Battalion

527
00:27:00,800 --> 00:27:03,320
can become the ace battalion of the 396th Brigade.

528
00:27:03,760 --> 00:27:06,600
The ace battalion of the entire Group Army!

529
00:27:08,320 --> 00:27:09,080
Comrades,

530
00:27:10,040 --> 00:27:10,960
to be honest,

531
00:27:11,680 --> 00:27:13,080
the Battalion Commander's three new initiatives

532
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:14,800
haven't really taken off yet.

533
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:17,760
But in my heart,

534
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:19,800
the flames

535
00:27:20,320 --> 00:27:21,800
have already started roaring.

536
00:27:22,800 --> 00:27:24,720
I am 120 percent convinced that

537
00:27:25,880 --> 00:27:27,280
as long as our First Battalion,

538
00:27:27,280 --> 00:27:28,560
all officers and soldiers,

539
00:27:28,960 --> 00:27:30,200
work together as one,

540
00:27:30,800 --> 00:27:32,400
in our military readiness,

541
00:27:32,720 --> 00:27:34,480
we can definitely turn things around.

542
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:36,920
And we can definitely bring the Invincible Battalion

543
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:39,000
banner back to us!

544
00:27:55,200 --> 00:27:55,920
Report.

545
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:02,160
Come in.

546
00:28:06,400 --> 00:28:07,360
Battalion Commander, sir.

547
00:28:07,480 --> 00:28:08,760
I have objections

548
00:28:09,120 --> 00:28:09,800
to your arrangements today.

549
00:28:11,200 --> 00:28:11,960
What objections?

550
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:15,400
Why make me a battalion staff officer?

551
00:28:18,280 --> 00:28:20,280
Why shouldn't you be a battalion staff officer?

552
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:22,600
Even if I offended you,

553
00:28:23,200 --> 00:28:24,680
you don't have to be so vindictive,

554
00:28:24,760 --> 00:28:26,240
and retaliate against me so soon.

555
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:27,680
I heard

556
00:28:28,040 --> 00:28:29,560
you've actually been pulling strings

557
00:28:30,280 --> 00:28:32,120
to get into headquarters as an administrative staff officer.

558
00:28:32,600 --> 00:28:33,600
That's my business.

559
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:35,120
It's none of your concern.

560
00:28:35,120 --> 00:28:36,800
You are currently in the 1st Battalion,

561
00:28:37,040 --> 00:28:38,280
which means you are my man.

562
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:39,800
Of course it's my concern.

563
00:28:41,040 --> 00:28:41,640
What do you mean?

564
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:43,480
Didn't you want to be a staff officer?

565
00:28:43,760 --> 00:28:45,280
I cleared a spot for you.

566
00:28:45,400 --> 00:28:46,200
Isn't that generous enough?

567
00:28:46,320 --> 00:28:48,480
You're making me lead the Blue Force detachment.

568
00:28:48,800 --> 00:28:50,760
Isn't that obviously setting me up to be hated?

569
00:28:50,760 --> 00:28:52,240
So what if you get cursed at a bit?

570
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:57,160
The Blue Force is the whetstone for troop training.

571
00:28:57,960 --> 00:28:58,760
In these coming months,

572
00:28:58,960 --> 00:29:00,560
the more hatred you draw,

573
00:29:00,800 --> 00:29:03,080
the more our battalion's combat awareness and readiness

574
00:29:03,080 --> 00:29:03,920
will improve.

575
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:05,400
Don't try to fool me with nice words.

576
00:29:05,640 --> 00:29:06,320
I'm not doing it.

577
00:29:06,560 --> 00:29:07,800
And I don't want to stay in the 1st Battalion anymore.

578
00:29:08,720 --> 00:29:09,520
Li Songwei!

579
00:29:11,200 --> 00:29:12,200
You think you can do whatever you want,

580
00:29:12,200 --> 00:29:13,080
and leave whenever you want?

581
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:15,400
What do you think my 1st Battalion is?

582
00:29:15,640 --> 00:29:17,400
We clearly don't see eye to eye anyway.

583
00:29:17,760 --> 00:29:18,840
You look down on me too,

584
00:29:19,600 --> 00:29:20,840
so there's no point in me staying here.

585
00:29:21,800 --> 00:29:23,160
I do look down on you.

586
00:29:24,680 --> 00:29:26,360
Do you know what I despise the most?

587
00:29:27,400 --> 00:29:28,920
It's that you're a sore loser.

588
00:29:30,960 --> 00:29:32,000
Let me tell you the truth.

589
00:29:32,120 --> 00:29:33,880
Transferring out of the 1st Battalion is impossible.

590
00:29:34,480 --> 00:29:36,240
You either do a good job

591
00:29:36,240 --> 00:29:37,120
leading the Blue Force detachment,

592
00:29:37,360 --> 00:29:38,840
or the Group Army's combat exercise,

593
00:29:38,840 --> 00:29:40,040
you can forget about participating in it.

594
00:29:41,400 --> 00:29:42,040
Get out!

595
00:29:49,880 --> 00:29:50,920
As if I can't handle you.

596
00:29:57,320 --> 00:29:58,520
This record is way too high.

597
00:30:00,280 --> 00:30:00,960
Done training?

598
00:30:20,160 --> 00:30:20,840
At ease!

599
00:30:21,680 --> 00:30:22,600
Attention!

600
00:30:27,760 --> 00:30:28,640
Battalion Commander,

601
00:30:28,960 --> 00:30:30,160
First Company is conducting tactical training.

602
00:30:30,160 --> 00:30:30,880
Awaiting your orders!

603
00:30:31,200 --> 00:30:31,720
At ease.

604
00:30:32,200 --> 00:30:32,640
Yes, sir!

605
00:30:34,960 --> 00:30:35,400
At ease!

606
00:30:36,480 --> 00:30:37,120
Xu Zhiqiang!

607
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:37,960
Here!

608
00:30:39,360 --> 00:30:40,120
Where is Li Songwei?

609
00:30:40,480 --> 00:30:41,240
Reporting to the Commander,

610
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:41,840
the Company Commander is sick.

611
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:43,400
Sick?

612
00:30:43,840 --> 00:30:45,080
What's wrong? Is it serious?

613
00:30:46,200 --> 00:30:46,800
It's nothing.

614
00:30:47,240 --> 00:30:48,080
He just needs some rest.

615
00:30:50,280 --> 00:30:51,000
Resume your training.

616
00:30:51,280 --> 00:30:51,800
Yes, sir!

617
00:30:55,560 --> 00:30:56,960
Looks like he's in a mood.

618
00:30:57,720 --> 00:31:00,040
His pride must have taken a hit.

619
00:31:00,640 --> 00:31:01,640
When you first arrived,

620
00:31:02,400 --> 00:31:03,680
he wanted to show you who's boss.

621
00:31:04,160 --> 00:31:04,760
But in the end,

622
00:31:04,760 --> 00:31:06,200
he made a fool of himself.

623
00:31:07,640 --> 00:31:08,640
Plus,

624
00:31:08,640 --> 00:31:10,080
he was up for Deputy Battalion Commander,

625
00:31:10,400 --> 00:31:11,360
but it didn't happen.

626
00:31:12,560 --> 00:31:13,560
Then I'll go check on him.

627
00:31:15,880 --> 00:31:16,760
In my opinion,

628
00:31:16,760 --> 00:31:17,640
at a time like this,

629
00:31:18,080 --> 00:31:19,160
it's best not to go.

630
00:31:19,440 --> 00:31:20,120
As for Li Songwei,

631
00:31:20,120 --> 00:31:21,320
I know him quite well.

632
00:31:21,440 --> 00:31:22,240
Dealing with him

633
00:31:22,520 --> 00:31:23,680
is like taming a horse.

634
00:31:24,160 --> 00:31:25,880
The wilder the horse is,

635
00:31:26,080 --> 00:31:27,560
the more finesse you have to use.

636
00:31:28,120 --> 00:31:29,520
You have to straighten out his mindset.

637
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:30,360
Usually, that's the only way

638
00:31:30,520 --> 00:31:31,920
he'll become truly loyal in the end.

639
00:31:33,280 --> 00:31:33,760
All right.

640
00:31:34,200 --> 00:31:35,040
I'll take your advice.

641
00:31:35,600 --> 00:31:37,040
But you still need to look into it,

642
00:31:37,040 --> 00:31:38,520
and see if he's facing any difficulties.

643
00:31:38,640 --> 00:31:39,120
Okay.

644
00:31:43,200 --> 00:31:44,080
What's going on?

645
00:31:45,680 --> 00:31:46,240
Reporting to the Commander,

646
00:31:46,360 --> 00:31:47,280
it seems to have broken down.

647
00:31:47,440 --> 00:31:48,240
I'll go up and take a look.

648
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:48,960
No need, Commander.

649
00:31:49,080 --> 00:31:50,320
We just need Golden Right Foot to fix it.

650
00:31:51,480 --> 00:31:52,320
Golden Right Foot?

651
00:31:52,920 --> 00:31:54,160
You mean Wu Dongsheng?

652
00:31:54,440 --> 00:31:54,880
Yes, sir!

653
00:32:12,320 --> 00:32:13,000
Wu Dongsheng.

654
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:14,240
A fifteen-year veteran.

655
00:32:14,480 --> 00:32:15,560
He's the 396th Brigade's

656
00:32:15,560 --> 00:32:17,200
top reconnaissance squad leader.

657
00:32:17,600 --> 00:32:19,400
Besides his outstanding military skills,

658
00:32:19,400 --> 00:32:20,680
he's also a mechanics geek.

659
00:32:21,040 --> 00:32:23,480
Thanks to some equipment innovations,

660
00:32:23,560 --> 00:32:25,240
he's already been awarded two third-class merits.

661
00:32:25,760 --> 00:32:27,040
Two third-class merits?

662
00:32:28,720 --> 00:32:30,240
Then why wasn't he recommended for a commission?

663
00:32:32,880 --> 00:32:33,880
These merits...

664
00:32:34,520 --> 00:32:35,840
came a bit too late.

665
00:32:36,800 --> 00:32:37,680
He's past the age limit.

666
00:32:39,960 --> 00:32:41,080
That's such a pity.

667
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:43,360
Even though he can't be an officer,

668
00:32:43,840 --> 00:32:46,200
we're trying every possible way

669
00:32:46,200 --> 00:32:47,360
to keep him here.

670
00:32:47,520 --> 00:32:48,280
Fortunately,

671
00:32:48,520 --> 00:32:50,160
Commissar Kang made his stance clear,

672
00:32:50,520 --> 00:32:51,640
saying that no matter what,

673
00:32:51,880 --> 00:32:53,320
he must be kept in the 396th Brigade.

674
00:32:54,560 --> 00:32:55,440
That's great.

675
00:32:57,120 --> 00:32:58,480
If a talent like him were to leave,

676
00:32:58,680 --> 00:32:59,800
it would be a loss for the army.

677
00:33:00,880 --> 00:33:01,760
It's all fixed.

678
00:33:03,040 --> 00:33:03,800
Give it a try.

679
00:33:12,800 --> 00:33:13,280
It works.

680
00:33:13,600 --> 00:33:14,360
Continue training!

681
00:33:14,600 --> 00:33:15,080
Yes, sir!

682
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:18,240
Squad Leader Wu.

683
00:33:20,280 --> 00:33:20,800
Battalion Commander.

684
00:33:22,920 --> 00:33:24,040
Squad Leader Wu is a jack of all trades.

685
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:26,280
I'm just someone who can't sit idle.

686
00:33:26,600 --> 00:33:27,520
It's mainly because

687
00:33:27,640 --> 00:33:28,520
I've been a soldier for so long.

688
00:33:28,520 --> 00:33:29,840
Hanging around the barracks every day,

689
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:32,000
you pick up a thing or two just by watching.

690
00:33:32,640 --> 00:33:33,360
"An elder at home

691
00:33:33,360 --> 00:33:34,160
is a treasure to own."

692
00:33:34,400 --> 00:33:35,560
Same goes for our 1st Battalion.

693
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:37,360
Having a veteran like you around

694
00:33:38,080 --> 00:33:39,120
puts the Instructor and me

695
00:33:39,120 --> 00:33:39,880
at ease.

696
00:33:40,840 --> 00:33:42,200
Well, the elder part is true,

697
00:33:42,600 --> 00:33:44,520
but I'm hardly a treasure.

698
00:33:44,760 --> 00:33:45,640
Quite modest, aren't you.

699
00:33:46,640 --> 00:33:47,880
Your reconnaissance detachment

700
00:33:47,960 --> 00:33:49,640
will be getting some new equipment later.

701
00:33:49,880 --> 00:33:50,960
You'll need to really put your mind to it.

702
00:33:52,560 --> 00:33:53,480
I guarantee to complete the mission!

703
00:33:57,840 --> 00:33:58,880
Li Songwei!

704
00:33:58,880 --> 00:34:00,440
You're abusing your power for a personal grudge!

705
00:34:00,560 --> 00:34:01,800
You're pushing me too far!

706
00:34:01,920 --> 00:34:03,440
If I don't teach you a lesson today,

707
00:34:03,440 --> 00:34:05,560
you won't know what hit you!

708
00:34:10,760 --> 00:34:12,120
My conscience is clear,

709
00:34:12,360 --> 00:34:13,040
and my head is held high.

710
00:34:13,400 --> 00:34:14,880
If you want to start trouble, Dong Zhenguo,

711
00:34:15,120 --> 00:34:16,159
I'll take you on.

712
00:34:29,760 --> 00:34:30,639
Attention!

713
00:34:43,120 --> 00:34:43,679
Report!

714
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:44,480
Battalion Commander!

715
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:45,560
Battalion Commander!

716
00:34:46,239 --> 00:34:48,159
Staff Officer Li and Company Commander Dong are fighting.

717
00:34:49,159 --> 00:34:49,960
What's going on?

718
00:34:50,280 --> 00:34:51,159
The Blue Force detachment

719
00:34:51,320 --> 00:34:52,639
is inspecting the Second Company's combat readiness.

720
00:34:52,639 --> 00:34:53,560
Their demands are too strict.

721
00:34:53,639 --> 00:34:54,400
Company Commander Dong couldn't take it.

722
00:35:01,160 --> 00:35:02,080
Where is your Battalion Commander?

723
00:35:03,400 --> 00:35:04,040
Report!

724
00:35:09,760 --> 00:35:10,840
Deputy Brigade Commander,

725
00:35:11,200 --> 00:35:12,120
the Second Company of the First Battalion

726
00:35:12,120 --> 00:35:13,880
is undergoing a combat readiness inspection.

727
00:35:14,080 --> 00:35:14,920
Awaiting orders.

728
00:35:15,200 --> 00:35:16,760
Acting Battalion Commander Guo Zijian.

729
00:35:17,040 --> 00:35:17,840
Guo Zijian.

730
00:35:18,960 --> 00:35:20,520
Your Blue Force detachment

731
00:35:21,800 --> 00:35:23,080
has really made an impression.

732
00:35:24,040 --> 00:35:25,120
Two company commanders

733
00:35:26,320 --> 00:35:28,000
are at each other's throats.

734
00:35:29,160 --> 00:35:29,720
Report!

735
00:35:30,440 --> 00:35:32,120
Li Songwei is using the Blue Force as an excuse

736
00:35:32,120 --> 00:35:32,880
to settle a personal score

737
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:33,720
and make things difficult for the Second Company.

738
00:35:33,760 --> 00:35:34,400
Report!

739
00:35:34,560 --> 00:35:35,880
I am following the Battalion Commander's orders

740
00:35:35,880 --> 00:35:36,720
to conduct combat training.

741
00:35:36,720 --> 00:35:37,600
Both of you, shut up!

742
00:35:37,800 --> 00:35:38,240
Yes, sir!

743
00:35:38,440 --> 00:35:38,920
Yes, sir!

744
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:42,120
Deputy Brigade Commander,

745
00:35:43,520 --> 00:35:44,840
let me handle this.

746
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:46,800
Don't trouble yourself over such a small matter.

747
00:35:47,320 --> 00:35:48,120
A small matter?

748
00:35:48,920 --> 00:35:50,080
I don't consider it a small matter.

749
00:35:51,240 --> 00:35:51,920
Tell me,

750
00:35:52,520 --> 00:35:53,600
how do you plan to handle it?

751
00:35:59,760 --> 00:36:00,520
Criticism and education.

752
00:36:01,120 --> 00:36:01,760
What else?

753
00:36:02,320 --> 00:36:03,160
Guide everyone

754
00:36:03,280 --> 00:36:05,240
to properly view the Blue Force detachment's actions

755
00:36:05,600 --> 00:36:06,880
and reduce hostility.

756
00:36:07,560 --> 00:36:08,280
And then?

757
00:36:08,640 --> 00:36:09,200
Furthermore,

758
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:11,920
your two company commanders made fools of themselves.

759
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:14,120
Are we just going to let it slide?

760
00:36:14,440 --> 00:36:15,840
Then what do you suggest, Deputy Brigade Commander?

761
00:36:16,040 --> 00:36:17,680
I want to hear what you suggest.

762
00:36:20,960 --> 00:36:21,960
Report, Deputy Brigade Commander.

763
00:36:22,040 --> 00:36:22,560
Speak.

764
00:36:23,080 --> 00:36:24,240
What I mean is,

765
00:36:24,440 --> 00:36:25,640
regarding the Blue Force detachment,

766
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:27,840
for their approach to realistic training,

767
00:36:27,960 --> 00:36:28,800
we should give them recognition.

768
00:36:29,120 --> 00:36:30,320
As for some comrades

769
00:36:30,560 --> 00:36:32,120
who are hostile toward the Blue Force,

770
00:36:32,280 --> 00:36:33,680
we should provide proper guidance.

771
00:36:33,920 --> 00:36:34,560
Third,

772
00:36:34,960 --> 00:36:36,480
we must carefully study the combat scenarios

773
00:36:36,680 --> 00:36:38,280
to make the training more realistic

774
00:36:38,480 --> 00:36:39,920
and closer to actual combat.

775
00:36:40,560 --> 00:36:41,080
Is that all?

776
00:36:41,320 --> 00:36:41,880
That is all.

777
00:36:42,480 --> 00:36:43,400
Guo Zijian!

778
00:36:44,040 --> 00:36:45,800
Is this how you manage troop training?

779
00:36:45,960 --> 00:36:47,080
Report, Deputy Brigade Commander.

780
00:36:47,400 --> 00:36:48,560
Regarding troop training,

781
00:36:48,800 --> 00:36:50,280
the syllabus only provides standards

782
00:36:50,280 --> 00:36:51,400
and general guidelines.

783
00:36:51,760 --> 00:36:53,000
As for specific training methods,

784
00:36:53,120 --> 00:36:54,080
it doesn't specify

785
00:36:54,280 --> 00:36:55,240
detailed rules.

786
00:36:55,680 --> 00:36:56,440
I believe

787
00:36:56,920 --> 00:36:58,840
as long as it boosts training enthusiasm

788
00:36:59,200 --> 00:37:00,600
and raises training standards,

789
00:37:00,920 --> 00:37:02,160
whether it's a short sword or a long sword,

790
00:37:02,360 --> 00:37:03,560
as long as it wins tough battles,

791
00:37:03,640 --> 00:37:04,680
it's a good sword.

792
00:37:04,720 --> 00:37:05,640
That concludes my report.

793
00:37:19,760 --> 00:37:21,320
Look at these two soldiers of yours.

794
00:37:37,800 --> 00:37:39,120
That kid Dong Zhenguo

795
00:37:39,120 --> 00:37:40,840
is pretty ruthless.

796
00:37:59,920 --> 00:38:00,480
What?

797
00:38:01,720 --> 00:38:03,280
Need me to apply the medicine myself?

798
00:38:12,720 --> 00:38:14,400
If you want to say thanks, just say it.

799
00:38:16,080 --> 00:38:17,800
Who said anything about thanks?

800
00:38:20,200 --> 00:38:21,200
Suit yourself.

801
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:23,240
Then let's have a chat

802
00:38:23,680 --> 00:38:24,960
about the Deputy Battalion Commander promotion.

803
00:38:27,560 --> 00:38:29,480
I didn't have to explain this to you,

804
00:38:30,040 --> 00:38:31,480
but I don't want you holding a grudge.

805
00:38:32,880 --> 00:38:33,800
In terms of seniority,

806
00:38:34,080 --> 00:38:34,800
years of service,

807
00:38:35,120 --> 00:38:35,880
and

808
00:38:35,880 --> 00:38:36,840
combat bravery,

809
00:38:36,920 --> 00:38:37,720
you have no issues.

810
00:38:38,080 --> 00:38:38,840
You're fully qualified.

811
00:38:39,840 --> 00:38:40,960
But in your theory

812
00:38:41,560 --> 00:38:43,640
and new equipment operation tests,

813
00:38:44,520 --> 00:38:45,600
your scores were less than ideal.

814
00:38:46,440 --> 00:38:47,320
You want to say

815
00:38:47,680 --> 00:38:49,600
theory and new equipment operation

816
00:38:49,880 --> 00:38:50,880
aren't important to you.

817
00:38:50,880 --> 00:38:51,400
Right?

818
00:38:51,920 --> 00:38:52,720
Let me tell you something.

819
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:55,520
If you don't pass these two,

820
00:38:56,080 --> 00:38:57,760
the new combat modes of the future...

821
00:38:57,760 --> 00:38:58,920
You won't be able to adapt to them at all.

822
00:38:59,680 --> 00:39:01,120
Think about it carefully.

823
00:39:06,760 --> 00:39:07,360
Alright.

824
00:39:09,160 --> 00:39:10,200
Wipe that look off your face.

825
00:39:10,200 --> 00:39:10,760
Come with me.

826
00:39:11,880 --> 00:39:12,440
Where to?

827
00:39:12,720 --> 00:39:13,560
Cut the crap.

828
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:14,560
Follow orders.

829
00:39:14,560 --> 00:39:15,040
Let's go.

830
00:39:22,360 --> 00:39:23,640
Daddy's here! Daddy's here!

831
00:39:23,920 --> 00:39:24,680
Daddy!

832
00:39:25,200 --> 00:39:26,120
Daddy!

833
00:39:26,880 --> 00:39:28,360
Daddy! Daddy!

834
00:39:28,760 --> 00:39:29,440
Dagou!

835
00:39:29,720 --> 00:39:30,600
Xiaoshao!

836
00:39:30,600 --> 00:39:33,600
Daddy! Daddy!

837
00:39:33,760 --> 00:39:35,040
Your wife and kids are here.

838
00:39:35,200 --> 00:39:36,400
Why are you just standing there?

839
00:39:36,400 --> 00:39:36,920
Go on.

840
00:39:40,760 --> 00:39:42,080
Dagou!

841
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:43,080
Xiaoshao!

842
00:39:44,280 --> 00:39:45,360
Why are you here?

843
00:39:47,080 --> 00:39:47,920
Did you miss Daddy?

844
00:39:47,920 --> 00:39:48,480
We did!

845
00:39:49,240 --> 00:39:49,960
Give Daddy a kiss.

846
00:39:52,080 --> 00:39:52,800
Good kids.

847
00:39:54,080 --> 00:39:54,840
Why are you here?

848
00:39:55,680 --> 00:39:56,840
Battalion Commander Guo

849
00:39:56,840 --> 00:39:57,800
wanted me to surprise you.

850
00:40:21,480 --> 00:40:21,960
Battalion Commander.

851
00:40:22,640 --> 00:40:23,080
Have a seat.

852
00:40:24,800 --> 00:40:26,000
Commander, what are these?

853
00:40:26,400 --> 00:40:27,400
These are

854
00:40:27,400 --> 00:40:29,280
treasures I collected back in the military academy.

855
00:40:29,680 --> 00:40:30,400
There are books,

856
00:40:30,400 --> 00:40:31,880
and some of the latest papers.

857
00:40:32,440 --> 00:40:33,840
I see you are

858
00:40:34,320 --> 00:40:35,120
quite interested in this area,

859
00:40:35,440 --> 00:40:36,200
and have a talent for it.

860
00:40:36,760 --> 00:40:37,600
As for these books,

861
00:40:38,040 --> 00:40:39,240
regarding your future development,

862
00:40:39,240 --> 00:40:40,080
they will all be helpful.

863
00:40:40,400 --> 00:40:41,080
So,

864
00:40:41,080 --> 00:40:41,800
I'm giving them to you.

865
00:40:42,280 --> 00:40:43,040
Thank you, Commander.

866
00:40:44,360 --> 00:40:44,920
Also,

867
00:40:44,920 --> 00:40:47,080
regarding your personal advancement,

868
00:40:47,440 --> 00:40:48,400
what are your thoughts?

869
00:40:53,320 --> 00:40:53,920
Commander,

870
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:56,680
I'm well into my thirties now.

871
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:58,000
Way past the age limit.

872
00:40:58,560 --> 00:40:59,520
Besides,

873
00:40:59,640 --> 00:41:00,840
in the entire army,

874
00:41:00,920 --> 00:41:02,440
where would you find a thirty-year-old new platoon leader?

875
00:41:02,960 --> 00:41:04,200
So I haven't thought much about it.

876
00:41:04,640 --> 00:41:06,000
I heard from the Instructor that

877
00:41:06,320 --> 00:41:08,000
regarding your retention and placement,

878
00:41:08,520 --> 00:41:10,200
the Brigade Party Committee already has a clear opinion.

879
00:41:10,840 --> 00:41:12,120
Commander, to be honest,

880
00:41:12,760 --> 00:41:14,200
I really don't care much about that.

881
00:41:15,640 --> 00:41:16,720
Then what do you care about?

882
00:41:18,600 --> 00:41:20,800
I just want to be a solid veteran.

883
00:41:21,640 --> 00:41:22,360
That's it.

884
00:41:25,400 --> 00:41:27,040
Commander, you really stumped me just now.

885
00:41:28,600 --> 00:41:29,680
To tell you the truth,

886
00:41:30,320 --> 00:41:31,560
I've been in the army for so many years,

887
00:41:31,560 --> 00:41:32,520
I'm used to everything here.

888
00:41:33,080 --> 00:41:34,080
If I left the army,

889
00:41:34,560 --> 00:41:35,800
I wouldn't know what to do.

890
00:41:36,040 --> 00:41:36,920
And I'd have no direction.

891
00:41:38,200 --> 00:41:39,520
But since you arrived,

892
00:41:40,080 --> 00:41:41,040
and especially

893
00:41:41,680 --> 00:41:43,400
after doing that exercise with you,

894
00:41:43,800 --> 00:41:44,560
I felt

895
00:41:44,800 --> 00:41:46,080
that was real combat.

896
00:41:46,400 --> 00:41:47,200
That was thrilling.

897
00:41:47,200 --> 00:41:48,200
That was awesome.

898
00:41:48,920 --> 00:41:49,360
So,

899
00:41:49,520 --> 00:41:50,200
I feel like

900
00:41:51,120 --> 00:41:52,520
I seem to have a direction now.

901
00:41:53,360 --> 00:41:54,000
I think

902
00:41:54,880 --> 00:41:56,040
I just want to be

903
00:41:56,360 --> 00:41:57,320
on the battlefield,

904
00:41:57,440 --> 00:41:58,640
a veteran fighting tough battles.

905
00:41:59,000 --> 00:41:59,440
Commander,

906
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:01,680
from now on, I'll wake up early every day

907
00:42:01,680 --> 00:42:02,280
and train more,

908
00:42:02,400 --> 00:42:03,280
for fear of falling behind.

909
00:42:03,440 --> 00:42:04,720
I'll just be waiting for you to call,

910
00:42:04,720 --> 00:42:05,200
"Wu Dongsheng!"

911
00:42:05,360 --> 00:42:05,800
"Here!"

912
00:42:05,880 --> 00:42:06,800
"Wu Dongsheng!" "Here!"

913
00:42:07,240 --> 00:42:08,720
I just want to fight alongside you.

914
00:42:10,240 --> 00:42:11,440
I understand what you mean.

915
00:42:13,400 --> 00:42:14,120
I promise you.

916
00:42:15,360 --> 00:42:16,000
In the First Battalion,

917
00:42:16,080 --> 00:42:17,440
as long as I, Guo Zijian, am here,

918
00:42:17,440 --> 00:42:18,560
you, Wu Dongsheng, will be here too.

919
00:42:19,280 --> 00:42:20,720
This feeling you mentioned

920
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:22,560
is exactly what I've been looking for

921
00:42:22,560 --> 00:42:23,800
and wanting to create.

922
00:42:24,640 --> 00:42:25,840
I won't let you down.

923
00:42:26,240 --> 00:42:26,840
Then Commander,

924
00:42:27,560 --> 00:42:28,320
keep your word.

925
00:42:29,080 --> 00:42:29,880
I'll keep my word.

926
00:42:32,040 --> 00:42:32,640
Study hard.

927
00:42:32,640 --> 00:42:33,120
Will do.

928
00:42:33,560 --> 00:42:34,320
Take care, Commander.

929
00:42:47,720 --> 00:42:48,400
Battalion Commander!

930
00:42:48,880 --> 00:42:50,360
A fight broke out in the mess hall.

931
00:42:50,680 --> 00:42:51,960
They're itching for a beating.
